# but world-readable over HTTP because the server runs as root), four
# installer/boot ISOs, and three *-rootfs.img files. The replacement keeps
# the approved rootfs fetch (exact ^[0-9a-f]{64}-rootfs\.img$ names on the
# same guest-reachable address) and denies listings, QCOW2, ISO, traversal,
# subpaths, symlinks, and non-GET/HEAD methods by construction.
#
